DECISIONS 202, CODEGEN.md §3.4 (the C++ name plan, decision 37): a record named `double` derives a C++ class named by a keyword, which C++ cannot declare, refused once at the record.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A pair.
record double {
  /// Its left.
  left: Int
}

emit cpp { out: "@features/a", namespace: "a", mode: data }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8011]  a/a.canon:4:8
  double is not a valid cpp identifier for @cpp(name:)

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
